---
title: Home
---

<section class="hero">
  <p class="eyebrow">Ruby on Rails Wizardry</p>
  <h1><%= site.title %></h1>
  <p class="lede"><%= site.tagline %></p>
  <p>
    <%= link_to "Open the tree", "/learn/", class: "button" %>
    <%= link_to "Open the library", "/docs/", class: "button button--ghost" %>
    <%= link_to "Pick a profile", "/docs/profiles/", class: "button button--ghost" %>
  </p>
</section>

<section class="grid" aria-label="Start here">
  <article class="card">
    <h2>What do I study next</h2>
    <p>
      A knowledge tree, not a locked course. Open any node.
    </p>
    <p><%= link_to "Knowledge tree", "/learn/" %></p>
  </article>

  <article class="card">
    <h2>Which bar applies</h2>
    <p>
      Federal ICT is Revised 508 (WCAG 2.0 AA plus ICT chapters).
      State and local web is ADA Title II (WCAG 2.1 AA).
      Current practice is WCAG 2.2 AA. Those are different checklists.
    </p>
    <p><%= link_to "Requirement profiles", "/docs/profiles/" %></p>
  </article>

  <article class="card">
    <h2>Work with an agent</h2>
    <p>
      Name a profile and a surface. Load only the criteria that apply.
      Do not dump the whole standard into one prompt.
    </p>
    <p><%= link_to "Reducing cognitive load", "/docs/agents/" %></p>
  </article>

  <article class="card">
    <h2>Official texts, nearby</h2>
    <p>
      Local markdown copies of W3C, Access Board, GSA, and DOJ material,
      each with a source URL, status, and license notice.
    </p>
    <p><%= link_to "Library map", "/docs/" %> · <%= link_to "Sources", "/docs/SOURCES/" %></p>
  </article>
</section>

<section data-controller="disclose" data-action="toggle->disclose#toggle">
  <h2>Official standards at a glance</h2>
  <p>One profile at a time. Open a card, then follow its local files.</p>

  <details data-disclose-target="item" open>
    <summary>Revised Section 508 — WCAG 2.0 A + AA</summary>
    <p>
      Binds U.S. federal agencies and ICT they develop, procure, maintain, or use.
      Technical bar is WCAG 2.0 Level A + AA, plus ICT hardware / software / authoring / support chapters.
    </p>
    <p><%= link_to "Revised standards", "/docs/section-508/" %></p>
  </details>

  <details data-disclose-target="item">
    <summary>ADA Title II web and mobile — WCAG 2.1 AA</summary>
    <p>
      Binds U.S. state and local governments (and contractors providing their services).
      After the 2026 IFR, compliance dates are 26 Apr 2027 (≥50k) and 26 Apr 2028 (smaller / special districts).
    </p>
    <p><%= link_to "Title II web and mobile", "/docs/ada/" %></p>
  </details>

  <details data-disclose-target="item">
    <summary>Current WCAG practice — 2.2 AA</summary>
    <p>
      Latest WCAG 2 Recommendation (also ISO/IEC 40500:2025).
      Content that meets 2.2 also meets 2.1 and 2.0 (with the 4.1.1 Parsing note).
    </p>
    <p><%= link_to "WCAG overview", "/docs/wcag/" %></p>
  </details>

  <details data-disclose-target="item">
    <summary>Enhanced / AAA</summary>
    <p>
      Selected Level AAA criteria. Optional; W3C does not recommend requiring AAA for entire sites.
    </p>
    <p><%= link_to "Conformance", "/docs/wcag/conformance/" %></p>
  </details>
</section>
